    "knowledge_point": "Estimating a Derivative Given Data or Tables Using a Central Difference Approximation",
    "problem": "Given that $f(9.6)=3$ and $f(10.4)=11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(10).$",
    "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=10$ with the step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(10) & ≈\\frac{f(10+0.4)-f(10-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10.4)-f(9.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-3}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{0.8} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
